# Publish GitHub Pages after commit and push

When the user asks to **commit and push** (or a commit-and-push action succeeds), also refresh the hosted app at https://ashevchuk.github.io/switchlab/ (repo https://github.com/ashevchuk/switchlab).

## Steps (after a successful push to the default branch)

1. `npm run build:dist-file`
2. Publish `dist-file/` to the `gh-pages` branch (force-push orphan publish is OK for this repo):

```bash
npm run build:dist-file
rm -rf /tmp/switchlab-gh-pages && mkdir -p /tmp/switchlab-gh-pages
cp -a dist-file/. /tmp/switchlab-gh-pages/
cd /tmp/switchlab-gh-pages && git init && git checkout -b gh-pages
git add -A && git commit -m "Publish dist-file build for GitHub Pages."
git remote add origin https://github.com/ashevchuk/switchlab.git
git push -f origin gh-pages
```

3. Confirm the live URL: https://ashevchuk.github.io/switchlab/

Skip Pages publish only if the user explicitly says not to, or the push was not to this repo / not meant for the live site.
